a93994d0-7335-43b1-ab8c-5a2c469d3df3	0424b954-a41f-4d8a-b204-72af6257e3d9	Development	development-noida-entry-r-kavach-ft9o	b9a82472-a279-4837-bfab-36891a41d93b	FULL_TIME	\N	ONSITE	1c7d522f-ea16-45b5-8add-7036ecbdf7a1	ENTRY	Overview\nWe are seeking an enthusiastic AIGP (AI Governance & Policy) Trainer to join our development team at an entry level. This role offers an exciting opportunity to design, develop, and deliver training programs that educate professionals on AI governance, security best practices, and policy implementation. You will work with cutting-edge technologies while helping organizations build a culture of AI security awareness and compliance.\n\nKey Responsibilities\n\n• Develop comprehensive training curricula focused on AI governance, security protocols, and organizational policy frameworks\n\n• Create engaging training materials including presentations, documentation, case studies, and hands-on exercises for diverse audiences\n\n• Deliver training sessions to technical and non-technical stakeholders, adapting content to different experience levels and learning styles\n\n• Collaborate with cybersecurity and policy teams to ensure training content aligns with industry standards and emerging threats\n\n• Gather feedback from training participants and continuously improve course content and delivery methods\n\n• Stay current with AI security trends, governance frameworks, and regulatory requirements to maintain training relevance\n\nRequired Qualifications\n\n• Bachelor's degree in Cybersecurity, Information Technology, Computer Science, or related field\n\n• Strong understanding of cybersecurity fundamentals, including risk management, threat assessment, and security controls\n\n• Excellent written and verbal communication skills with the ability to explain complex concepts clearly\n\n• Demonstrated ability to work collaboratively in team environments and manage multiple priorities\n\n• Foundational knowledge of AI concepts, machine learning basics, or policy frameworks is a plus\n\nPreferred Qualifications\n\n• CompTIA Security+, CEH (Certified Ethical Hacker), or equivalent cybersecurity certification\n\n• Previous experience in training delivery, instructional design, or corporate training environments\n\n• Familiarity with AI governance frameworks such as NIST AI RMF or ISO/IEC standards\n\nWhat We Offer\n\n• Professional Development: Comprehensive training and certification support to advance your cybersecurity expertise and career growth\n\n• Collaborative Culture: Work alongside experienced security professionals and contribute to meaningful projects that impact organizational security posture\n\n• Flexible Work Environment: Access to modern tools and resources to deliver effective training across multiple formats\n\n• Career Advancement: Clear pathways to grow from entry-level trainer to senior training specialist or security specialist roles	SCREENING	\N	[{"id": "q_1784181718866343", "type": "MULTIPLE_CHOICE", "options": ["higih", "jvjg", "jvug"], "question": "gxydyfu", "required": true}]	PENDING	\N	\N	\N	0	0	\N	\N	2026-07-16 06:02:18.075	2026-07-16 06:02:18.075
0fc3e204-4952-408f-a051-43c273c5a10e	d4a7d601-57d2-4a9d-a69c-5452a72cf593	Cybersecurity & Compliance Internship	cybersecurity-compliance-internship-remote-entry-rivedix-technology-solutions-kltt	beccd270-1bb0-4a9a-ba35-5e316b20c9a6	INTERNSHIP	\N	REMOTE	\N	ENTRY	<h3>Overview</h3><p>We are seeking a motivated and detail-oriented Data Privacy Trainer to join our Cybersecurity &amp; Compliance team as an intern. In this entry-level role, you will develop and deliver engaging training programs on data privacy best practices, compliance regulations, and security awareness to employees across the organization. This is an excellent opportunity to launch your cybersecurity career while making a meaningful impact on organizational security culture.</p><h3>Key Responsibilities</h3><ul><li><p>Design and develop data privacy training materials, including presentations, documentation, and interactive modules aligned with industry standards and regulatory requirements</p></li><li><p>Deliver engaging training sessions to diverse employee groups, ensuring clear communication of complex compliance concepts and privacy principles</p></li><li><p>Assist in conducting privacy impact assessments and compliance audits to identify training gaps and opportunities for improvement</p></li><li><p>Support the creation and maintenance of privacy policies and procedures documentation</p></li><li><p>Track training completion rates and effectiveness metrics, providing reports and recommendations to senior compliance staff</p></li><li><p>Stay current with evolving data protection regulations (GDPR, CCPA, HIPAA) and incorporate updates into training programs</p></li></ul><h3>Required Qualifications</h3><ul><li><p>Currently enrolled in or recently completed a degree program in Cybersecurity, Information Technology, Business, Law, or related field</p></li><li><p>Strong understanding of data privacy principles, compliance frameworks, and regulatory requirements</p></li><li><p>Excellent written and verbal communication skills with the ability to explain technical concepts to non-technical audiences</p></li><li><p>Demonstrated ability to work independently and collaboratively in a team environment</p></li><li><p>Foundational knowledge of cybersecurity fundamentals and information security best practices</p></li></ul><h3>Preferred Qualifications</h3><ul><li><p>Relevant certifications such as CISSP, CIPP/US, or CompTIA Security+ in progress or completed</p></li><li><p>Previous experience in training delivery, instructional design, or compliance-related roles</p></li><li><p>Familiarity with learning management systems (LMS) and training development tools</p></li></ul><h3>What We Offer</h3><ul><li><p><strong>Professional Development:</strong> Hands-on experience in cybersecurity and compliance with mentorship from industry experts, helping you build a strong foundation for your career</p></li><li><p><strong>Flexible Learning Environment:</strong> Exposure to real-world compliance challenges and the opportunity to earn industry-recognized certifications with company support</p></li><li><p><strong>Competitive Compensation:</strong> Competitive hourly rate and potential for conversion to full-time opportunities based on performance</p></li><li><p><strong>Collaborative Culture:</strong> Work alongside dedicated security professionals in a supportive environment that values innovation and continuous learning</p></li></ul><p></p>	DIRECT	\N	\N	EXPIRED	\N	\N	\N	259	7	2026-07-06 09:08:32.25	2026-05-07 09:08:32.25	2026-05-07 07:26:31.86	2026-07-07 00:00:00.634
3b2dd011-f9b1-4f80-85dc-a2f676766134	d4a7d601-57d2-4a9d-a69c-5452a72cf593	Cybersecurity Intern	cybersecurity-intern-remote-entry-rivedix-technology-solutions-uwi6	e0378fe5-0e4f-4f40-bc1a-4adb27fc2689	INTERNSHIP	\N	REMOTE	\N	ENTRY	<h3>Overview</h3><p>We are seeking a motivated and detail-oriented <strong>Cybersecurity Intern</strong> to join our Security Operations team. This entry-level position offers hands-on experience in identifying, analyzing, and mitigating cybersecurity threats. You will work alongside experienced security professionals to support our organization's mission of protecting critical assets and data from evolving cyber threats.</p><h3>Key Responsibilities</h3><ul><li><p>Assist in monitoring network traffic and security logs to identify suspicious activities and potential security incidents</p></li><li><p>Support vulnerability assessments and penetration testing activities under the guidance of senior security staff</p></li><li><p>Help maintain and update security documentation, policies, and incident response procedures</p></li><li><p>Participate in security awareness training initiatives and support user education programs</p></li><li><p>Conduct preliminary analysis of security alerts and escalate findings to appropriate team members</p></li><li><p>Assist with security tool configuration, deployment, and maintenance across the organization</p></li></ul><h3>Required Qualifications</h3><ul><li><p>Currently enrolled in or recently completed an undergraduate degree in Computer Science, Information Technology, Cybersecurity, or related field</p></li><li><p>Strong foundational knowledge of networking concepts (TCP/IP, DNS, HTTP/HTTPS) and operating systems (Windows, Linux)</p></li><li><p>Familiarity with cybersecurity principles including encryption, authentication, and access control</p></li><li><p>Excellent problem-solving skills and ability to work effectively in a team environment</p></li><li><p>Strong communication skills and attention to detail</p></li></ul><h3>Preferred Qualifications</h3><ul><li><p>Relevant cybersecurity certifications such as CompTIA Security+, CompTIA Network+, or CEH (Certified Ethical Hacker)</p></li><li><p>Experience with security information and event management (SIEM) platforms or intrusion detection systems</p></li><li><p>Hands-on experience with penetration testing tools or vulnerability scanning software</p></li></ul><h3>What We Offer</h3><ul><li><p>Comprehensive mentorship from experienced cybersecurity professionals in a collaborative environment</p></li><li><p>Practical exposure to industry-standard security tools and technologies</p></li><li><p>Flexible work arrangements to accommodate academic schedules</p></li><li><p>Competitive internship compensation and potential for full-time conversion upon successful completion</p></li></ul><p></p>	DIRECT	\N	\N	APPROVED	\N	\N	\N	447	14	2026-08-07 09:01:09.077	2026-06-08 09:01:09.077	2026-04-23 06:14:22.903	2026-08-02 16:04:23.52
0accab72-3166-4a31-b8c3-eaafd4d9c207	0424b954-a41f-4d8a-b204-72af6257e3d9	VAPT Analyst	vapt-analyst-remote-entry-r-kavach-ija1	d80af742-3a94-4389-b7fa-1d255487c8b1	INTERNSHIP	\N	REMOTE	\N	ENTRY	Overview\nWe are seeking a motivated VAPT (Vulnerability Assessment and Penetration Testing) Analyst to join our cybersecurity team. In this entry-level role, you will conduct security assessments, identify vulnerabilities, and provide actionable recommendations to strengthen our clients' security posture. This is an excellent opportunity to launch your career in ethical hacking and penetration testing while working alongside experienced security professionals.\n\nKey Responsibilities\n\n• Perform vulnerability assessments and penetration tests on client networks, applications, and infrastructure using industry-standard tools\n\n• Identify, document, and classify security vulnerabilities with detailed severity ratings and business impact analysis\n\n• Develop and execute test plans based on client requirements and scope definitions\n\n• Create comprehensive penetration testing reports with findings, evidence, and remediation recommendations\n\n• Communicate technical findings to both technical and non-technical stakeholders in a clear and professional manner\n\n• Assist in vulnerability remediation efforts and conduct retesting to verify fixes\n\nRequired Qualifications\n\n• Bachelor's degree in Computer Science, Information Technology, Cybersecurity, or related field (or equivalent professional experience)\n\n• Strong foundational knowledge of networking, operating systems, and web application security\n\n• Hands-on experience with penetration testing tools such as Burp Suite, Metasploit, Nmap, or similar platforms\n\n• Solid understanding of common vulnerabilities including OWASP Top 10, SQL injection, cross-site scripting, and privilege escalation\n\n• Excellent written and verbal communication skills with ability to document findings professionally\n\nPreferred Qualifications\n\n• CompTIA Security+, CEH (Certified Ethical Hacker), or OSCP (Offensive Security Certified Professional) certification\n\n• Previous internship or practical experience in cybersecurity, penetration testing, or security operations\n\n• Familiarity with scripting languages such as Python, Bash, or PowerShell\n\nWhat We Offer\n\n• Professional Development: Comprehensive training program, certification sponsorship, and mentorship from senior security professionals to accelerate your career growth\n\n• Competitive Compensation: Attractive salary package with performance bonuses and benefits\n\n• Career Growth: Clear advancement opportunities within our growing cybersecurity division with exposure to diverse projects and clients\n\n• Collaborative Environment: Work with a talented team of security experts in a supportive, innovation-driven culture	DIRECT	\N	[]	PENDING	\N	\N	\N	0	0	\N	\N	2026-07-03 09:35:19.521	2026-07-03 09:35:19.521
acead5ca-33d2-47ef-95bd-3de12eb1b39e	0424b954-a41f-4d8a-b204-72af6257e3d9	VAPT Analyst	vapt-analyst-remote-entry-r-kavach-dead	d80af742-3a94-4389-b7fa-1d255487c8b1	INTERNSHIP	\N	REMOTE	\N	ENTRY	Overview\nWe are seeking a motivated VAPT (Vulnerability Assessment and Penetration Testing) Analyst to join our cybersecurity team. In this entry-level role, you will conduct security assessments, identify vulnerabilities, and provide actionable recommendations to strengthen our clients' security posture. This is an excellent opportunity to launch your career in ethical hacking and penetration testing while working alongside experienced security professionals.\n\nKey Responsibilities\n\n• Perform vulnerability assessments and penetration tests on client networks, applications, and infrastructure using industry-standard tools\n\n• Identify, document, and classify security vulnerabilities with detailed severity ratings and business impact analysis\n\n• Develop and execute test plans based on client requirements and scope definitions\n\n• Create comprehensive penetration testing reports with findings, evidence, and remediation recommendations\n\n• Communicate technical findings to both technical and non-technical stakeholders in a clear and professional manner\n\n• Assist in vulnerability remediation efforts and conduct retesting to verify fixes\n\nRequired Qualifications\n\n• Bachelor's degree in Computer Science, Information Technology, Cybersecurity, or related field (or equivalent professional experience)\n\n• Strong foundational knowledge of networking, operating systems, and web application security\n\n• Hands-on experience with penetration testing tools such as Burp Suite, Metasploit, Nmap, or similar platforms\n\n• Solid understanding of common vulnerabilities including OWASP Top 10, SQL injection, cross-site scripting, and privilege escalation\n\n• Excellent written and verbal communication skills with ability to document findings professionally\n\nPreferred Qualifications\n\n• CompTIA Security+, CEH (Certified Ethical Hacker), or OSCP (Offensive Security Certified Professional) certification\n\n• Previous internship or practical experience in cybersecurity, penetration testing, or security operations\n\n• Familiarity with scripting languages such as Python, Bash, or PowerShell\n\nWhat We Offer\n\n• Professional Development: Comprehensive training program, certification sponsorship, and mentorship from senior security professionals to accelerate your career growth\n\n• Competitive Compensation: Attractive salary package with performance bonuses and benefits\n\n• Career Growth: Clear advancement opportunities within our growing cybersecurity division with exposure to diverse projects and clients\n\n• Collaborative Environment: Work with a talented team of security experts in a supportive, innovation-driven culture	DIRECT	\N	[]	PENDING	\N	\N	\N	0	0	\N	\N	2026-07-03 09:37:34.863	2026-07-03 09:37:34.863
