5f3e76a3-792f-497f-8247-5f008a934c01	d4a7d601-57d2-4a9d-a69c-5452a72cf593	IT System Engineer	it-system-engineer-pune-mid-rivedix-technology-solutions-mepb	d4e53f4c-267c-4d9f-adff-c4c8ff4b5b40	FULL_TIME	\N	ONSITE	d71f386e-398b-4fd1-aa5a-31e6e09774fa	MID	<p>Job description Key Responsibilities: • Design and set up Active Directory and Organizational Units (OU). • Configure Windows Domain, including security groups, group policies, and computer policies. • Implement role-based access control using domain security policies. • Install, configure, and manage Acronis backup and restore solutions. • Deploy and configure McAfee / Trillix endpoint protection, including AV, file integrity, application control, DLP, ePO, and dashboards. • Configure FortiSIEM, implement use cases, and manage security event monitoring. • Configure and harden managed switches (Cisco, Hirschmann, Palo Alto), including port mirroring. • Establish Windows domain trust relationships and integrate with McAfee ePO. • Set up and configure AAA/Radius servers for authentication and policies. • Deploy and manage Network Management Systems (SolarWinds, WhatsUp Gold). • Implement local security policies, system hardening, and configure security logs and event IDs. • Set up WSUS and manage patch deployment systems. • Configure Next-Generation Firewalls (NGFW), including ACLs, interfaces, rules, • SIEM integration</p>	DIRECT	\N	\N	APPROVED	\N	\N	\N	696	6	2026-08-07 09:01:14.978	2026-06-08 09:01:14.978	2026-03-11 05:48:09.515	2026-08-05 06:16:50.113
910ecae4-44bd-40f3-b7ef-8566e7e7c481	d4a7d601-57d2-4a9d-a69c-5452a72cf593	Product Service Engineer (Medical Device)	product-service-engineer-medical-device-pune-mid-rivedix-technology-solutions-d39s	260024fb-8f2b-44bc-a04a-51a35f0a67f2	FULL_TIME	\N	ONSITE	d71f386e-398b-4fd1-aa5a-31e6e09774fa	MID	<p>We are seeking a Cybersecurity Engineer to support the Security &amp; Privacy Advisor in ensuring the ongoing security, safety, and regulatory compliance of deployed medical and safety-critical devices. This role focuses on post-market cybersecurity surveillance, vulnerability assessment, and risk management across embedded systems and connected devices. The engineer will analyze security vulnerabilities, assess potential functional and patient-safety impacts, support patch and remediation strategies, and collaborate with cross-functional teams to maintain compliance with industry standards and regulatory requirements.</p>	DIRECT	\N	\N	CLOSED	\N	Role Cancelled	2026-04-14 06:46:00.668	537	3	2026-04-12 11:18:15.261	2026-03-13 11:18:15.261	2026-03-13 11:17:58.214	2026-04-14 06:46:00.669
4b71d62d-3b22-436e-beaa-c6eba8dd8b6b	d4a7d601-57d2-4a9d-a69c-5452a72cf593	CISSP Trainer	cissp-trainer-remote	f2c68b02-2dbd-4503-a888-76a4441794f4	CONTRACT	\N	REMOTE	\N	SENIOR	<h2>About the Role</h2>\n<p>We are looking for a certified CISSP professional to train candidates preparing for the CISSP certification exam. The trainer will deliver comprehensive training covering all eight domains of the CISSP Common Body of Knowledge (CBK), including Security and Risk Management, Asset Security, Security Architecture, Communications and Network Security, IAM, Security Assessment, Security Operations, and Software Development Security.</p>\n\n<h3>Key Responsibilities</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Deliver comprehensive training on all 8 CISSP domains</li>\n<li>Develop study materials aligned with latest exam objectives</li>\n<li>Conduct engaging online sessions with real-world scenarios</li>\n<li>Provide practice questions and mock exams</li>\n<li>Share effective test-taking strategies and exam tips</li>\n<li>Explain complex security concepts using practical examples</li>\n<li>Guide students through Common Body of Knowledge (CBK)</li>\n<li>Track student progress and provide personalized feedback</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>Requirements</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>4+ years of experience in information security leadership roles</li>\n<li>Active CISSP certification holder (mandatory)</li>\n<li>Deep knowledge of all 8 CISSP domains</li>\n<li>Proven track record of successful student outcomes</li>\n<li>Excellent presentation and teaching skills</li>\n<li>Ability to simplify complex security concepts</li>\n<li>Understanding of current CISSP exam format and requirements</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>Required Certifications</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>CISSP (Certified Information Systems Security Professional) - Mandatory</li>\n<li>CISM (Certified Information Security Manager) - Preferred</li>\n<li>CISA (Certified Information Systems Auditor) - Preferred</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>What We Offer</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Flexible remote work schedule</li>\n<li>Competitive contract rates</li>\n<li>High demand for CISSP training</li>\n<li>Opportunity to help professionals advance their careers</li>\n<li>Access to latest CISSP study materials and resources</li>\n</ul>	DIRECT	\N	null	CLOSED	\N	Role Cancelled	2026-02-26 04:14:06.63	32	1	2026-03-16 11:40:19.278	2026-02-14 11:40:19.278	2026-02-14 11:40:19.279	2026-02-26 04:14:06.631
