6fee79a4-9844-4b4c-b066-6da932bf657f	2e523ed5-73af-4eaf-a22f-8200a9da4c6b	System Engineer	Tata Consultancy Services	Hyderabad	Full-time	2022-02	\N	t	An SAP Security and GRC Consultant designs, implements, and manages secure SAP environments (ECC, S/4HANA, Fiori) and governs access to prevent risks. Key roles include developing authorization roles, managing user provisioning, configuring SAP GRC Access Control (ARA, ARM, EAM), and performing SOD (Segregation of Duties) analysis for compliance. They ensure compliance with regulatory standards (e.g., SOX) and troubleshoot authorization errors.	{"SAP GRC, ECC, FIORI"}	{}	2026-02-11 02:08:29.503	2026-02-11 02:08:29.503
bee5417d-b9e9-4d12-80aa-a03a1b8befb0	0c4bbc1d-01a5-42fe-a35e-695983c92818	Package Specialist SAP Security and GRC	IBM	Bengaluru	Full-time	2023-07	2026-02	f	As a SAP Security and GRC consultant, I mainly work with the Identity and Access administration constituting few important responsibilities such as:\n\n1. User Administration & Access Support:\n----------\nManage full life cycle of user administration via SU01, SU10, modification, mass provisioning, locking/unlocking, password resets, and onboarding/offboarding.\n\n2. Authorization, Role Management & Risk Analysis:\n----------\nDesign, build and maintain authorization roles using PFCG; conduct authorization tracing and troubleshooting with SU53, SU56, and STAUTHTRACE to resolve access issues efficiently, user and role risk analysis as per SoD conflicts, assisting with mitigation or remediation.\n\n3. ECC to HANA Migration:\n----------\nCreate roles and users with the existing access from ECC to HANA system by coordinating with functional teams. Hyper care support during go-live.\n\n4. GRC Access Control Operations:\n----------\nAdminister Access Request Management (ARM), Emergency Access Management (EAM), and Role Management (BRM), assisting with access issues of User Provisioning workflows and firefighter IDs\n\n5. Audit Compliance & Governance:\n----------\nSupport audit requirements with sample data, audit trail collection and justification meetings (e.g., SM19/SM20, SUIM reports, AGR_USERS, USR02). Coordinated monthly and quarterly reviews, backups, migrations, and drill mock testing, along with event and team-building activities.\n\n6. Client Engagement, Support & Training Delivery:\n----------\nAct as technical point of contact for access request issues. Provide end-user support during backups, upgrades, and migration activities. Delivered 2-3 group trainings (GHs) for 8 members across project teams, translating SAP Security concepts. \n\n7. Technical & Operational Fluency:\n----------\nGUI scripting for various IAM tasks and basic job scheduling. Experience across project support, go‑live support, hyper care, and continuous operations in both support and implementation modalities	{"SAP Security","SAP GRC","Power BI",AWS,Excel}	{}	2026-02-11 07:34:14.456	2026-02-11 07:34:14.456
2ddd2807-8be3-4b30-9dde-e140cbb3cf84	59af4e8b-27f5-45b7-a1a0-789b8dc9ca41	Associate	Cognizant	Hyderabad	Full-time	2022-10	\N	t	SAP Security and GRC Consultant with 3+ years of experience at Cognizant, supporting global clients like PepsiCo. \n\nSkilled in user administration, role design, authorization troubleshooting, and compliance management across SAP ECC, BW, and HANA systems.\n\nWorked on Emergency Access Management (EAM), Access Risk Analysis (ARA), Access Request Management (ARM), and Business Role Management (BRM) within SAP GRC. Identified and resolved Segregation of Duties (SoD) conflicts during user/role provisioning using risk analysis and simulations in SAP GRC. \nBasic knowledge in SAP fiori like tiles, catalogs, groups and Odata services.	{"SAP User Administration","SAP role Administrator","SAP GRC Access Control","SAP Fiori"}	{}	2026-02-11 12:49:02.525	2026-02-11 12:49:02.525
