82e05195-8e00-4cf5-98c2-e4769f83b98f	19f0c404-7859-4987-afa4-00081247d263	SOC Analyst Home Lab Environment	Designed and building a multi-machine cybersecurity lab environment to simulate real-world enterprise SOC monitoring and detection workflows.\n\nEnvironment includes:\n\n• pfSense firewall/router for network segmentation and traffic control\n• Suricata IDS/IPS for intrusion detection and alert generation\n• Wazuh SIEM for centralized log collection and security monitoring\n• Kali Linux for authorized security testing scenarios\n• Windows Server Active Directory domain environment\n• Windows 10 endpoint system for user activity simulation\n• Vulnerable lab machines for controlled attack simulations\n\nProject focus:\n\n• Log analysis and alert triage workflows\n• Network traffic analysis using Wireshark\n• Threat detection aligned with MITRE ATT&CK techniques\n• Understanding attacker behavior in safe lab environments\n• Building foundational SOC analyst skills\n\nPurpose:\nDevelop hands-on experience with tools and processes used by real Security Operations Centers (SOC) to detect, investigate, and respond to threats.	{pfsense,suricata,wazuh,"kali linux",wireshark,"windows server","active directory",virtualBox,TCP/IP,Linux}		2026-02	\N	t	{}	2026-03-23 14:07:17.568	2026-03-23 14:07:17.568
